# `≤1 p.xsd:decimal` with two DataHasValue witnesses of xsd:integer (1 and 2).
# The integers are decimals (OWL 2 §4.1), so A has two distinct values under a
# ≤1 over decimals — UNSATISFIABLE. rustdl reports A satisfiable with
# `incomplete: false` and `dropped: {}`: integer and decimal values are counted
# in separate card_sat buckets and never against each other.
#
# Adjudicated: HermiT 1.4.5 calls A unsatisfiable. Konclude is NOT used here: it
# treats integer and decimal as one value space (recorded in CLAUDE.md), so its
# agreement would not be independent.
#
# This fixture took over the acceptance set's detection when #334 made
# `dkey-maxcard-oneof` agree with its oracle (the guard's FIFTH firing:
# chainrange -> chaincompose -> invfunc-inverse -> dkey-maxcard-oneof -> this).
# Verified on the harness's own surface before committing: `unsat=[]`,
# `dropped={}`, `incomplete=false`.
provenance: hermit   # HermiT 1.4.5, #334 work (2026-10-23)
unsatisfiable: A
